1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:02:01,488
Transcription by CastingWords

2
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:31,488
Transcription by CastingWords

3
00:02:31,508 --> 00:03:01,488
Transcription by CastingWords

4
00:03:01,508 --> 00:03:31,488
Transcription by CastingWords

5
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,488
She's been in the hospital forever.

6
00:03:34,208 --> 00:03:37,388
I feel bad for him. He's been alone all this time.

7
00:03:37,668 --> 00:03:39,168
Father won't forgive you, you know.

8
00:03:39,848 --> 00:03:40,768
Excuse me?

9
00:03:40,768 --> 00:03:53,308
What makes you think that I've forgiven him? I still remember. He branded his own daughter a failure when she was a middle school student.

10
00:03:53,308 --> 00:04:02,668
He said there are other things in life than Shogi. As if he really believed that.

11
00:04:02,668 --> 00:04:07,328
But what he said is true. There are other things in life than Shogi.

12
00:04:07,328 --> 00:04:25,728
Don't you lie to me too! Shogi is the only thing you and Dad ever think about. I've had enough of this. The way that you look at me. You make me feel like I'm a loser. You both always tiptoe around me.

13
00:04:25,728 --> 00:04:37,568
It's infuriating. I hate it. Both of you judging me. How long do I have to feel this pathetic?

14
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:48,888
Then I'll leave instead. If I go, I'm sure that no one will really worry about me.

15
00:04:48,888 --> 00:04:59,108
But it's different with you. You are important to Father. Even if you don't realize it.

16
00:04:59,108 --> 00:05:09,748
In all things, the path should have a teacher or not.

17
00:05:09,748 --> 00:05:19,288
10 a.m. The game's starting. The tournament final to determine who the challenger will be for the Shishio title. It's the first of three matches.

18
00:05:20,508 --> 00:05:27,208
Right now, gathered in the special match room, the two players are facing each other.

19
00:05:29,108 --> 00:05:35,608
I wonder what kind of battle it'll be.

20
00:05:38,448 --> 00:05:43,568
When I was playing against Mr. Shimada, a strange feeling came over me.

21
00:05:44,708 --> 00:05:51,388
It was like I'd stepped into a sea of trees and became entangled by something powerful.

22
00:05:52,828 --> 00:05:56,368
It was like something silently tightening around me.

23
00:05:56,368 --> 00:06:01,288
What kind of game will he play when he goes up against Goto?

24
00:06:03,708 --> 00:06:07,668
Um, excuse me. Here are my absence notices for March.

25
00:06:08,208 --> 00:06:11,568
Oh, Kiriyama. Look at this. It's amazing.

26
00:06:12,328 --> 00:06:12,648
Huh?

27
00:06:12,648 --> 00:06:15,128
Two hours in and this is where they're at.

28
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:17,728
So, there.

29
00:06:19,728 --> 00:06:26,848
One look and I could tell by the moves they had played already that this was going to be an all-out slugfest.

30
00:06:26,848 --> 00:06:33,828
I was wondering how those two would stack up against each other. It looks like they're going blow for blow.

31
00:06:34,948 --> 00:06:35,988
They're crazy.

32
00:06:41,268 --> 00:06:41,708
Hmm.

33
00:06:43,388 --> 00:06:44,488
You should go.

34
00:06:46,568 --> 00:06:47,608
Go where, sir?

35
00:06:47,808 --> 00:06:48,908
To Shogi Hall.

36
00:06:48,908 --> 00:06:50,488
Uh, but...

37
00:06:50,488 --> 00:06:54,168
This isn't a title match, so they won't be updating the blog in real time.

38
00:06:54,528 --> 00:06:57,408
Wouldn't it be more educational if you were there watching it in person?

39
00:06:58,188 --> 00:06:59,888
But I have so many absences.

40
00:07:02,468 --> 00:07:02,988
Ow!

41
00:07:04,388 --> 00:07:05,888
It's fine! Just go!

42
00:07:05,888 --> 00:07:12,448
He does have enough days, right?

43
00:07:13,028 --> 00:07:14,988
One, two, three...

44
00:07:14,988 --> 00:07:15,288
Yeah.

45
00:07:15,728 --> 00:07:17,728
He'll barely make it, I think.

46
00:07:17,888 --> 00:07:18,948
What am I doing?

47
00:07:19,088 --> 00:07:20,128
I'm an awful teacher!

48
00:07:20,128 --> 00:07:20,448
Huh?

49
00:07:30,928 --> 00:07:32,108
Hey, Kiriyama.

50
00:07:32,788 --> 00:07:33,268
Kiriyama?

51
00:07:35,888 --> 00:07:38,188
Oh, look!

52
00:07:38,508 --> 00:07:39,428
Gold to 4-3!

53
00:07:39,968 --> 00:07:40,748
No way.

54
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:42,968
I've never seen Mr. Shimada like this.

55
00:07:43,428 --> 00:07:43,788
Oh?

56
00:07:44,508 --> 00:07:46,448
Is he sacrificing his bishop?

57
00:07:47,448 --> 00:07:49,808
I've never seen him play like this before, either.

58
00:07:52,808 --> 00:07:55,888
It felt like their presence came from the special match room,

59
00:07:56,248 --> 00:07:58,668
then made its way through the dark hallway,

60
00:07:59,348 --> 00:08:00,948
and now could be felt in this room.

61
00:08:00,948 --> 00:08:01,028
Oh, my God!

62
00:08:05,888 --> 00:08:11,148
Why?

63
00:08:11,148 --> 00:08:12,148
How?

64
00:08:12,148 --> 00:08:27,468
What's so different?

65
00:08:27,468 --> 00:08:31,388
Why are each of their moves so fascinating?

66
00:08:38,828 --> 00:08:40,888
Is it the amount of time they've been playing?

67
00:08:43,848 --> 00:08:45,968
The depth of experience they had acquired?

68
00:08:45,968 --> 00:08:50,508
The weight of all of their sacrifices?

69
00:08:52,228 --> 00:08:54,528
Or is it all of the above?

70
00:08:59,728 --> 00:09:00,548
That's right.

71
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:01,908
These two.

72
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:07,488
They have complete faith in their own abilities.

73
00:09:09,488 --> 00:09:11,948
A battle of will.

74
00:09:16,028 --> 00:09:18,068
The match ended at 9pm,

75
00:09:18,748 --> 00:09:20,748
when Shimada Eighth Den conceded defeat.

76
00:09:21,948 --> 00:09:22,728
That was it.

77
00:09:23,508 --> 00:09:26,428
The first game of the Shishio Championship Finals Tournament,

78
00:09:26,428 --> 00:09:29,568
and Goto Ninth Den is the winner.

79
00:09:33,648 --> 00:09:34,428
Hey, Rei.

80
00:09:41,068 --> 00:09:43,008
This place hasn't changed a bit.

81
00:09:43,228 --> 00:09:44,808
It's such a dreary building.

82
00:09:45,628 --> 00:09:46,908
I used to hate it here,

83
00:09:47,428 --> 00:09:48,648
on this dark street,

84
00:09:49,048 --> 00:09:50,748
as well as that gloomy shrine.

85
00:09:52,108 --> 00:09:52,528
Kyoko.

86
00:09:52,528 --> 00:09:52,648
Kyoko.

87
00:09:52,648 --> 00:09:52,728
Kyoko.

88
00:09:56,428 --> 00:10:01,148
Well, if it isn't my two stalkers here together.

89
00:10:02,228 --> 00:10:03,348
What now, Kyoko?

90
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:06,308
Well, after all, I...

91
00:10:06,308 --> 00:10:09,468
And you?

92
00:10:10,068 --> 00:10:12,328
You were just raring to take me on, huh?

93
00:10:13,708 --> 00:10:15,108
Shimada knocked you out.

94
00:10:15,788 --> 00:10:16,508
What happened?

95
00:10:18,088 --> 00:10:20,088
Never underestimate A-class.

96
00:10:26,428 --> 00:10:30,988
Wait, are you really leaving?

97
00:10:32,148 --> 00:10:33,728
I didn't want to leave.

98
00:10:34,648 --> 00:10:36,068
Hey, wait a minute!

99
00:10:40,148 --> 00:10:41,208
Are you running?

100
00:10:42,288 --> 00:10:43,248
Away from me?

101
00:10:44,228 --> 00:10:44,708
But,

102
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:47,108
I couldn't be with her anymore.

103
00:10:47,108 --> 00:10:47,168
I couldn't be with her anymore.

104
00:10:47,168 --> 00:10:52,888
I was in a hurry to grow up.

105
00:10:56,128 --> 00:10:58,788
I thought if I couldn't stand on my own two feet,

106
00:10:59,788 --> 00:11:05,148
then there was no way I could protect them.

107
00:11:09,088 --> 00:11:10,768
Those who meant the most to me.

108
00:11:10,768 --> 00:11:17,888
I didn't win.

109
00:11:18,488 --> 00:11:21,328
I tried to push with the one-turn-loss bishop exchange,

110
00:11:21,548 --> 00:11:23,648
but that bastard fought back immediately.

111
00:11:24,388 --> 00:11:25,328
He was cheerful.

112
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,728
That old man really is tough.

113
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:29,888
Him and that scary face.

114
00:11:30,888 --> 00:11:32,648
For someone so strong,

115
00:11:32,728 --> 00:11:34,048
he's surprisingly childish.

116
00:11:36,168 --> 00:11:36,688
Still,

117
00:11:36,688 --> 00:11:40,208
I swear I won't lose next time.

118
00:11:42,168 --> 00:11:42,648
Yeah!

119
00:11:43,088 --> 00:11:44,648
I know you can do it!

120
00:11:56,828 --> 00:11:57,728
I see.

121
00:11:58,068 --> 00:11:58,928
That's tough.

122
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:02,468
I can see why he's stayed away.

123
00:12:03,188 --> 00:12:03,608
Mm-hmm.

124
00:12:04,128 --> 00:12:06,328
He made promises to you girls,

125
00:12:06,328 --> 00:12:08,028
but then he failed to deliver.

126
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:10,508
It's hard for a young boy.

127
00:12:11,008 --> 00:12:11,748
At his age,

128
00:12:11,768 --> 00:12:13,288
it can be almost mortifying.

129
00:12:13,808 --> 00:12:14,048
Ah!

130
00:12:16,268 --> 00:12:17,488
If it were me,

131
00:12:17,588 --> 00:12:18,908
I'd slit my belly.

132
00:12:18,968 --> 00:12:19,268
Well,

133
00:12:19,328 --> 00:12:20,108
if it were me,

134
00:12:20,188 --> 00:12:22,088
I'd seclude myself up in the mountains.

135
00:12:22,488 --> 00:12:22,888
Ah!

136
00:12:24,568 --> 00:12:25,088
Really?

137
00:12:25,888 --> 00:12:27,268
It's that embarrassing?

138
00:12:28,688 --> 00:12:30,988
But it wouldn't change the way we see him.

139
00:12:31,648 --> 00:12:33,228
He said he'd try his hardest,

140
00:12:33,508 --> 00:12:35,568
so I'm sure he did all he could.

141
00:12:35,568 --> 00:12:36,888
That's how he is.

142
00:12:37,608 --> 00:12:39,268
Even if it didn't work out,

143
00:12:39,628 --> 00:12:41,068
no one would laugh at him.

144
00:12:41,908 --> 00:12:42,428
Exactly.

145
00:12:42,948 --> 00:12:44,808
Shame can strengthen you.

146
00:12:44,828 --> 00:12:45,008
Huh?

147
00:12:45,128 --> 00:12:46,548
Because if you should fail,

148
00:12:46,648 --> 00:12:48,208
it means you've challenged yourself.

149
00:12:49,428 --> 00:12:50,868
That's a hell of a lot better

150
00:12:50,868 --> 00:12:52,028
than a life of doing nothing

151
00:12:52,028 --> 00:12:53,428
but laughing at other people.

152
00:12:53,428 --> 00:12:56,008
The thing is,

153
00:12:56,208 --> 00:12:57,548
the kid is still young

154
00:12:57,548 --> 00:12:59,188
and too damn serious.

155
00:12:59,648 --> 00:13:02,268
He must have really wanted to beat that other guy.

156
00:13:03,148 --> 00:13:06,148
I've never seen Ray show so much fighting spirit before.

157
00:13:06,408 --> 00:13:07,708
He was so fired up.

158
00:13:07,708 --> 00:13:08,888
Yeah.

159
00:13:09,568 --> 00:13:09,928
Well,

160
00:13:10,008 --> 00:13:11,908
I guess he bit off more than he could chew.

161
00:13:17,548 --> 00:13:19,188
I bet all he's eating now

162
00:13:19,188 --> 00:13:21,128
is just sweet buns and ramen, huh?

163
00:13:22,208 --> 00:13:23,708
What do you think we should do?

164
00:13:23,948 --> 00:13:24,888
I feel sad.

165
00:13:24,888 --> 00:13:27,348
You just gotta leave him be for now.

166
00:13:28,108 --> 00:13:30,508
The only way to make up for a blunder at work

167
00:13:30,508 --> 00:13:32,188
is to work harder to fix it.

168
00:13:32,768 --> 00:13:35,008
Until he comes to terms with what happened,

169
00:13:35,368 --> 00:13:36,248
he'll be stuck.

170
00:13:36,688 --> 00:13:37,468
In the meantime,

171
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:39,068
he'll have to try his best.

172
00:13:39,388 --> 00:13:41,548
He'll figure this stuff out when he's older.

173
00:13:41,808 --> 00:13:42,888
It's no big secret.

174
00:13:43,608 --> 00:13:45,048
Of all the people in the world

175
00:13:45,048 --> 00:13:46,528
who've put themselves out there,

176
00:13:46,528 --> 00:13:49,368
every one of them

177
00:13:49,368 --> 00:13:51,228
has been humiliated themselves

178
00:13:51,228 --> 00:13:52,528
at some point.

179
00:14:03,768 --> 00:14:05,228
Hey, Shimada.

180
00:14:05,608 --> 00:14:06,548
Seems to me

181
00:14:06,548 --> 00:14:09,428
that you look even older than I do.

182
00:14:10,628 --> 00:14:12,768
I don't know what you're talking about.

183
00:14:13,388 --> 00:14:14,768
It must be pretty difficult

184
00:14:14,768 --> 00:14:16,248
for a man your age

185
00:14:16,248 --> 00:14:17,728
to try and stay in shape.

186
00:14:20,408 --> 00:14:21,308
Don't tell me

187
00:14:21,308 --> 00:14:22,968
you've been secretly working out.

188
00:14:23,348 --> 00:14:24,488
Must be tough

189
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:25,488
for a narcissist.

190
00:14:28,828 --> 00:14:30,828
You think so, chum?

191
00:14:32,428 --> 00:14:33,828
Shall we go now?

192
00:14:46,248 --> 00:14:49,368
That was so cool.

193
00:14:49,588 --> 00:14:51,488
They give off such a confident aura.

194
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:53,248
I wonder what they were saying.

195
00:14:53,368 --> 00:14:55,008
Shimada is so cool.

196
00:14:55,088 --> 00:14:56,028
So that's it.

197
00:14:56,288 --> 00:14:57,208
That's the kind of thing

198
00:14:57,208 --> 00:14:58,828
that happens when you make it to A class.

199
00:14:59,888 --> 00:15:00,748
That's strange.

200
00:15:01,088 --> 00:15:03,428
I can't smell the slightest bit of aura on me.

201
00:15:04,728 --> 00:15:05,808
Since I'm B1,

202
00:15:05,928 --> 00:15:07,268
do I have to move up to A class

203
00:15:07,268 --> 00:15:08,028
to smell like that?

204
00:15:08,028 --> 00:15:09,028
I bet that's it.

205
00:15:09,188 --> 00:15:10,848
That's when you'll have that aura, too.

206
00:15:11,148 --> 00:15:11,948
Come on, let's go.

207
00:15:12,588 --> 00:15:13,228
It's time.

208
00:15:13,488 --> 00:15:14,608
Their match is gonna start.

209
00:15:14,868 --> 00:15:15,248
Right.

210
00:15:15,768 --> 00:15:16,828
I don't think you guys

211
00:15:16,828 --> 00:15:18,048
will ever have it.

212
00:15:18,548 --> 00:15:19,628
At least not while you're

213
00:15:19,628 --> 00:15:20,888
spying behind bushes.

214
00:15:21,248 --> 00:15:21,528
Hmm.

215
00:15:21,528 --> 00:15:23,208
As you can see,

216
00:15:23,368 --> 00:15:24,848
Germany's strong recovery

217
00:15:24,848 --> 00:15:25,828
of productivity

218
00:15:25,828 --> 00:15:27,408
at the end of World War I

219
00:15:27,408 --> 00:15:28,608
It's almost 10 o'clock.

220
00:15:29,288 --> 00:15:30,508
The match is about to start.

221
00:15:31,808 --> 00:15:32,868
Three matches determine

222
00:15:32,868 --> 00:15:34,188
who goes to the championship.

223
00:15:35,168 --> 00:15:36,328
Goto Ninth Den

224
00:15:36,328 --> 00:15:37,448
won the first match.

225
00:15:38,648 --> 00:15:40,728
This is Mr. Shimada's last chance.

226
00:15:41,788 --> 00:15:42,968
During the previous match,

227
00:15:43,368 --> 00:15:45,068
they unexpectedly slugged it out.

228
00:15:46,708 --> 00:15:47,628
What kind of battle

229
00:15:47,628 --> 00:15:48,668
will it be this time?

230
00:15:49,728 --> 00:15:50,208
Damn it.

231
00:15:50,208 --> 00:15:52,128
I want to watch so badly.

232
00:15:53,048 --> 00:15:53,848
But I can't.

233
00:15:54,468 --> 00:15:54,868
Okay.

234
00:15:55,068 --> 00:15:56,748
I just finished calculating

235
00:15:56,748 --> 00:15:57,788
your attendance records.

236
00:15:58,428 --> 00:16:00,048
And I've come to the conclusion

237
00:16:00,048 --> 00:16:00,908
that you're not allowed

238
00:16:00,908 --> 00:16:01,588
to catch a cold

239
00:16:01,588 --> 00:16:02,888
or have an illness of any kind.

240
00:16:03,428 --> 00:16:04,368
You've already got

241
00:16:04,368 --> 00:16:05,548
two scheduled days off

242
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:06,548
for ranking competition,

243
00:16:06,688 --> 00:16:08,128
so we can't do anything about that.

244
00:16:08,868 --> 00:16:10,608
But if you happen to advance

245
00:16:10,608 --> 00:16:11,628
in any of the tournaments,

246
00:16:11,768 --> 00:16:13,008
you'll be at the edge of a cliff.

247
00:16:14,128 --> 00:16:15,908
Also, in case something should happen,

248
00:16:16,228 --> 00:16:17,768
aim to get higher than average scores

249
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:19,428
on all of the year-end tests, okay?

250
00:16:19,428 --> 00:16:21,508
As for what's going to be covered

251
00:16:21,508 --> 00:16:22,368
on those tests,

252
00:16:22,808 --> 00:16:24,188
I'd say you could ask a friend,

253
00:16:24,348 --> 00:16:25,708
but by the time you found one,

254
00:16:25,768 --> 00:16:26,748
the exam would be over.

255
00:16:27,408 --> 00:16:29,408
Instead, I asked all of the teachers

256
00:16:29,408 --> 00:16:30,968
for the materials on your behalf.

257
00:16:31,248 --> 00:16:32,528
Here, don't lose this.

258
00:16:33,488 --> 00:16:34,288
Okay, then.

259
00:16:34,428 --> 00:16:35,568
You've got to pass.

260
00:16:35,568 --> 00:16:36,688
If you don't,

261
00:16:36,748 --> 00:16:37,668
your classmates will start

262
00:16:37,668 --> 00:16:38,688
calling you old man.

263
00:16:38,948 --> 00:16:40,268
You're right, Mr. Hayashida.

264
00:16:40,588 --> 00:16:41,328
Thanks a lot.

265
00:16:41,888 --> 00:16:43,048
This is a big help.

266
00:16:46,468 --> 00:16:47,388
But now,

267
00:16:47,948 --> 00:16:50,548
why do I feel like crap?

268
00:16:50,548 --> 00:17:03,908
You're right.

269
00:17:03,908 --> 00:17:06,348
No!

270
00:17:33,908 --> 00:17:43,368
It's a slugfest. Again. Look at them. They're just so intense.

271
00:17:43,868 --> 00:17:46,788
In fact, they're using more brute force now than last time.

272
00:17:53,008 --> 00:17:57,408
No way. They're insane. They're using their kings to fight.

273
00:17:57,588 --> 00:18:00,108
Why? What are you guys doing? It's so immature.

274
00:18:00,388 --> 00:18:02,888
Who would think that playing the king would be a good way to win?

275
00:18:02,888 --> 00:18:04,028
It's completely reckless.

276
00:18:32,888 --> 00:18:38,028
That was real thunder. Now their pieces are glowing with electricity.

277
00:18:38,028 --> 00:18:43,168
Huh?

278
00:18:43,168 --> 00:18:49,028
Guess who won, kiddo?

279
00:18:49,028 --> 00:19:02,368
Guess who won, kiddo?

280
00:19:02,368 --> 00:19:06,508
Yes! I knew you'd win! That was awesome!

281
00:19:10,508 --> 00:19:13,088
After one match, he's exhausted!

282
00:19:13,088 --> 00:19:19,848
What's the matter, kiddo?

283
00:19:19,848 --> 00:19:22,088
Oh, it's just that...

284
00:19:22,088 --> 00:19:24,228
Kyriyama hasn't texted me back yet.

285
00:19:24,228 --> 00:19:26,228
I see.

286
00:19:26,228 --> 00:19:29,228
Maybe I went a little too far on the last match.

287
00:19:29,228 --> 00:19:30,368
Hmm...

288
00:19:42,368 --> 00:19:47,368
Tell me, why are you so interested in Kyriyama getting better?

289
00:19:47,368 --> 00:19:49,508
Well, I guess...

290
00:19:49,508 --> 00:19:51,508
Well, I guess...

291
00:19:51,508 --> 00:19:53,508
It's because he...

292
00:19:53,508 --> 00:19:56,828
He had the courage to knock me down.

293
00:19:57,428 --> 00:19:59,828
Then, he pulled me back up again.

294
00:19:59,828 --> 00:20:05,968
I spent a lot of time in the hospital when I was just a little kid.

295
00:20:05,968 --> 00:20:10,888
The only thing that got me through it was studying everything I could about Shogi.

296
00:20:10,888 --> 00:20:22,848
While all the other kids my age were outside having fun and playing, there I was, completely immersed in Shogi.

297
00:20:24,988 --> 00:20:30,528
And yet, the stronger I got, the more I would write off my weaker opponents.

298
00:20:31,028 --> 00:20:33,568
I thought they were just cowards that didn't try.

299
00:20:34,368 --> 00:20:37,068
It was so annoying and frustrating.

300
00:20:37,668 --> 00:20:38,788
I was sick of it.

301
00:20:38,788 --> 00:20:42,788
Then, when I was nothing but a lump of ego...

302
00:20:52,788 --> 00:20:53,788
Um...

303
00:20:53,788 --> 00:20:54,788
Here...

304
00:20:57,788 --> 00:20:58,788
Have some.

305
00:21:01,188 --> 00:21:02,788
That's when...

306
00:21:02,788 --> 00:21:04,788
I met Kyriyama.

307
00:21:04,788 --> 00:21:07,788
He knocked me to the ground.

308
00:21:08,788 --> 00:21:11,788
And saved me.

309
00:21:11,788 --> 00:21:15,788
There is someone stronger than me.

310
00:21:15,788 --> 00:21:18,788
Someone who's put in more effort than me.

311
00:21:18,788 --> 00:21:22,788
He made me realize that I'm not alone.

312
00:21:22,788 --> 00:21:25,788
I see.

313
00:21:25,788 --> 00:21:26,788
Hmm.

314
00:21:26,788 --> 00:21:27,788
I can understand that.

315
00:21:27,788 --> 00:21:28,788
Kinda.

316
00:21:28,788 --> 00:21:29,788
Wait a second!

317
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:30,788
Hey!

318
00:21:30,788 --> 00:21:31,788
Hey, come on!

319
00:21:31,788 --> 00:21:32,788
Wait a minute!

320
00:21:32,788 --> 00:21:33,788
Wait!

321
00:21:33,788 --> 00:21:34,788
Wait!

322
00:21:34,788 --> 00:21:35,788
Wait!

323
00:21:35,788 --> 00:21:36,788
Wait!

324
00:21:36,788 --> 00:21:40,788
Wait!

325
00:21:40,788 --> 00:21:41,788
Wait a' second!

326
00:21:41,788 --> 00:21:46,788
Wait!

327
00:21:47,288 --> 00:21:47,788
Wait!

328
00:21:47,788 --> 00:21:48,788
Ha ha ha!

329
00:21:49,788 --> 00:21:50,788
What the hell!

330
00:21:50,788 --> 00:21:59,228
What the hell?

331
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:01,128
Goto, you moron!

332
00:22:01,568 --> 00:22:03,528
That's it! I've had it with you!

333
00:22:04,208 --> 00:22:07,508
Wait, but Goto is a married man.

334
00:22:08,128 --> 00:22:08,968
Then who's that?

335
00:22:09,288 --> 00:22:11,968
She's so beautiful and young.

336
00:22:11,968 --> 00:22:13,668
Did they just have an argument?

337
00:22:20,788 --> 00:22:24,288
What is this sense of defeat?

338
00:22:25,568 --> 00:22:26,268
No!

339
00:22:26,708 --> 00:22:28,108
That was nothing at all!

340
00:22:28,488 --> 00:22:30,488
I'll win the next run too, dammit!

341
00:22:30,988 --> 00:22:33,088
Come on, kiddo. Let's get back.

342
00:22:33,368 --> 00:22:35,248
We have to plan for the final match!

343
00:22:35,448 --> 00:22:36,908
Yes! There it is!

344
00:22:37,048 --> 00:22:38,488
That's what I'm talking about!

345
00:22:38,488 --> 00:22:52,208
I'm sorry. You were actually already two days short.

346
00:22:52,508 --> 00:22:56,208
I see. It's okay. It's all my fault anyway.

347
00:22:57,788 --> 00:22:59,448
I'm the one who's sorry.

348
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:37,391
All right, then. What shall we do for the girls' festival at our house this year?

349
00:24:37,751 --> 00:24:39,291
Well, shall we get started?

350
00:24:39,951 --> 00:24:42,431
Oh, no. I completely forgot why I was here.

351
00:24:42,551 --> 00:24:45,551
If he doesn't want to come over to our house anymore, then fine.

352
00:24:45,891 --> 00:24:50,471
Hinawe Sushi, hurry up! Mama wants her right now! Right now!

353
00:24:51,931 --> 00:24:55,711
March comes in like a lion. Hey, you better watch it, too.

354
00:24:55,851 --> 00:24:58,991
I know. I get it already. You better not miss it, either.

355
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
Thank you.

